    "package_qualification": "Literal hash-linked routes only. Existing physical pin ownership applies; aliases share pads. PB3 SWO/JTDO conflicts with CRS and other alternate uses. Board wiring, population, signal quality and trace capture unqualified.",
    "contracts": [
      {
        "id": "freeze_condition",
        "detail": "Freeze requires CPU HALTED and selected STOP bit; when CPU runs, peripherals continue regardless of freeze bit. I2C/I3C controls concern listed timeout counters, not proven complete bus transaction suspension.",
        "evidence": [
          "RM0522:p2540",
          "RM0522:p2541"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "family_exclusions",
        "detail": "Absent-peripheral bits must remain reset. Broader RM tables do not admit TIM3/4/5/16/17, I2C2 or DMA channels4..7 on exact C542. APB1HFZR is reserved.",
        "evidence": [
          "header.freeze",
          "RM0522:p2541",
          "RM0522:p2544"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "low_power_behavior",
        "detail": "Debug retains clock/power and changes low-power behavior; peripherals may continue. Debug measurements do not qualify normal low-power current or timing. Standby exit causes system reset.",
        "evidence": [
          "RM0522:p2539",
          "RM0522:p2540",
          "RM0522:p2542",
          "RM0522:p2543"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "reset_scope",
        "detail": "RM states DBGMCU registers are not reset by system reset, only POR. Apply this to reviewed control/freeze state, not blindly to authentication fields: DBG_VALR VAL_RDY has explicit conditional system-reset clearing. No reset or restoration executed.",
        "evidence": [
          "RM0522:p2541",
          "RM0522:p2550"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "access_scope",
        "detail": "Software base0x44024000 and debugger base0xE00E4000 are distinct documented views. Authentication can restrict debugger access; ignored access is not successful configuration. Authentication/mailbox/password/option operations excluded.",
        "evidence": [
          "RM0522:p2541",
          "RM0522:p2542",
          "RM0522:p2543",
          "RM0522:p2548",
          "RM0522:p2549"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "SDK_ownership",
        "detail": "HAL freeze wrappers call LL atomic bit setters/clearers; low-power LL uses ordinary register bit operations. No saved-state ownership, cross-owner release, hardware halt verification, readback success or RTC erratum enforcement is supplied. APIs alone do not authorize altering a debug session.",
        "evidence": [
          "HAL.wrappers",
          "LL.freeze",
          "LL.low_power"
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "RTC_subsecond",
        "detail": "ES2.7.1: subsecond alarm downcounter remains clocked despite RTC freeze. With MASKSS nonzero and an alarm immediately before breakpoint/printf, ALRAF/ALRBF can repeatedly reassert and resist clearing. No workaround; freeze is not a complete RTC snapshot guarantee.",
        "evidence": [
          "ES0676:p2",
          "ES0676:p7"
        ]
      }
    ],
